  "description": "Lets a .tsx, .jsx or Lit component be an ordinary Rask component. Derive a component from ReactComponent or LitComponent, drop the front-end file beside it, and its props are declared in C# — the generator emits the TypeScript interface the file imports, so renaming a C# property stops the front end compiling. The live diff treats the island's subtree as opaque, because those nodes belong to its own renderer.",
